---
import BaseLayout from "../components/BaseLayout.astro";
import { absoluteUrl, href } from "../lib/paths";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "AboutPage",
  name: "About Dumpster Price Check",
  url: absoluteUrl("/about"),
  description:
    "How Dumpster Price Check reads dumpster rental prices, and what it leaves blank when a company does not publish a number.",
  isPartOf: {
    "@type": "WebSite",
    name: "Dumpster Price Check",
    url: absoluteUrl("/"),
  },
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About this price check"
  description="Dumpster Price Check is independent of the dumpster companies it lists. Here is how a price gets on the page, and how a wrong price is handled."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <p class="crumbs"><a href={href("/")}>Home</a> / About</p>
  <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
  <h1>How these dumpster prices are checked</h1>
  <div class="prose stack">
    <p>
      Dumpster Price Check is a comparison for people renting a dumpster in College Station or
      Bryan. It is not Aggieland Dumpster Rentals, BCS Junk Removal, Waste Falcon, Rocking H
      Dumpsters, Texas Disposal Systems, CTI Response, Pronto Services, Texas Commercial Waste,
      Bin There Dump That Aggieland, or BVR Waste and Recycling. It is not the City of College
      Station or the City of Bryan.
    </p>
    <h2>How a price gets on the page</h2>
    <p>
      A price, a size, a day count, or a fee is listed only when that company's own page states it.
      The row links that page and says Checked plus the day the page was read. That day is not a
      promise that the price is still current. If the page does not state a fact, the row says
      Not listed. If the page tells you to call, the price says Call for quote. Search snippets,
      ads, and review sites are not used as prices. No number on this site is an estimate.
    </p>
    <h2>When two pages disagree</h2>
    <p>
      Waste Falcon's marketing page says $45 per ton and $8 a day after day 7. The 20-yard and
      30-yard booking pages say $42 per ton and $8 a day after day 10. Those rows show the booking
      page and say the sources disagree. The 20-yard booking page also says up to 7 days are
      included, then $8 a day after day 10, and it does not say what days 8, 9, and 10 cost.
    </p>
    <p>
      Aggieland Dumpster Rentals does not state an exact yard size. The FAQ says the trailers
      average just under 20 yards. The size column does not say 20 yards, because that would be a
      guess. The homepage prices are plus tax. The tax amount is not published.
    </p>
    <p>
      BCS Junk Removal lists a dump fee of $60 per ton and does not state an included tonnage. The
      tons column says Not listed. It does not say 0 tons, because the page did not say 0.
    </p>
    <p>
      Rocking H Dumpsters lists 10, 20, 30, and 40 yard roll-offs at $295, $395, $495, and $595
      for up to 10 days. Tonnage is $32 or $73 per ton, and the page does not say which landfill
      rate applies. Included tons are not stated. A fuel surcharge is based on distance, and the
      amount is not published. Tax is not stated.
    </p>
    <h2>Sites that did not load</h2>
    <p>
      5 Star Dumpsters (5stardumps.com) and Aggregate Underground &amp; Turf (aggregateuat.com) did
      not load on Nov 19, 2026. They are not in the tables. No price was taken from an old listing
      or a search snippet.
    </p>
    <h2>Paid links</h2>
    <p>
      No link on this site is paid, and no affiliate program has been joined. If that changes, the
      link will say Sponsored. Open the company page before you pay. A price can change after the
      day on the row.
    </p>
    <h2>What you cannot do here</h2>
    <ul class="clean">
      <li>No accounts, no booking, and no payment.</li>
      <li>No ad trackers.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>A wrong price</h2>
    <p>
      This site has no contact form, no email address, and no phone number. Open the source link on
      the row and read the company page. The day on the row is the day that page was read.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
